The retrieved question was not supplied, so this summarises the factual evidence the ranked candidates contain. Duplicate candidates were merged, and the strongest evidence comes first.

1. **Planned changes to the PM document** (planning-SearchFlow-PM, eid_1f678d18): The team agreed on five changes:
   - add examples of the AI capabilities to Product Differentiation;
   - say how user feedback will be gathered in Product Development;
   - add data on Slack's search limitations to Market Opportunity;
   - describe the industry-event and testimonial plans in Go-to-Market;
   - mention the first beta feedback.
2. **UI pull request** (develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow, eid_4812cbd8): PR #28 (https://github.com/salesforce/SearchFlow/pull/28) changes how semantic search results are shown. It adds relevance scores and a way for users to give feedback.
3. **Limited customization** (planning-SearchFlow, eid_3bcf2a20): Customization is described as "quite basic". Users can't build complex search queries or change filters beyond a few preset options, which could limit teams with specific search needs.
4. **System Design Document** (planning-SearchFlow, eid_95f6d01c): The SearchFlow System Design Document was shared with the team for feedback.
5. **Name change** (planning-SearchFlow, eid_e96d2f38, and planning-AISearchforSlack, eid_fd8cecea): The product was first discussed as "AISearchforSlack", starting with a kickoff for its Product Vision Document. It was later called "SearchFlow", and a team member agreed that the new name "capture[s] the essence of the product better".

None of the sources contradict each other, and none of them give a publication date.
